  "adaptation": "Retain WinOne module namespace, unified configuration/logs/tray, recovery errors and PID-reuse protection. Reuse scoped Esc/native-close handling, script identity, original-window visibility and queued tray gestures. Existing WinOne native console creation retains its explicit environment/ownership handling. UI uses existing WinOne controls; program exit requires confirmation. Normal startup leaves original triggers alone; the selected mode derives the compatibility startup field, with custom scheduling independent; collected-icon single click still automatically adds a double click. No new dependency or standalone WinTray UI. Tray collection uses the same local WinTray receiving-end bridge; WinOne permits EPOCH/RESUME through its per-window UIPI filter for elevated operation and preserves native handshake errors instead of reporting every delivery failure as a timeout. The 2026-11-03 review keeps WinOne's explicit os.Process wait/exit-status callback for ShellExecuteEx scripts, preserves the fixture's no-foreground-activation constraint, and reuses transactional deselection for retryable maintenance before terminal collector shutdown. Portable WeChat opt-in settings round-trip without account data or credentials. Capability mapping and verification boundaries: docs/wintray-sync-20261103.md.",
